        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0e858e0e-63ba-5f81-bd55-1adf75f3ad1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Yorkshire Terrier, Cavalier King Charles Spaniel, Chihuahua, Papillon, Pointer\n- People: Ronald Reagan, Nancy Reagan\n- Organizations: The Kennel Club, American Kennel Club\n- Places: Yorkshire, England, United States\n- Concepts: Hypoplasia of dens\n- Animals: Rex\n\nFacts:\n- The Yorkshire Terrier was developed in Yorkshire, England, during the 19th century to catch rats in clothing mills.\n- The Yorkshire Terrier is a small dog breed of terrier type.\n- The Cavalier King Charles Spaniel is a small spaniel classified as a toy dog by The Kennel Club and the American Kennel Club.\n- Hypoplasia of dens is more commonly seen in the Chihuahua, the Papillon, the Pointer, and the Yorkshire Terrier.\n- Rex was born on December 16, 1984.\n- Rex was a Cavalier King Charles Spaniel owned by Ronald Reagan and Nancy Reagan during Ronald Reagan's term as President of the United States.\n- Rex died on August 31, 1998.",
